    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d178">

                <pb facs="0220" n="186" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg186"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-09-25"><hi rendition="#italic">September 25,
                        1897</hi></date>. (Received October 8.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 107.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 22, of July 8
                    last, I have the honor to transmit herewith a translation of a note and two
                    accompaniments which have to-day been received from the Imperial foreign office,
                    in which is contained a list of cases where trichinae have been found in pork or
                    pork products imported from the United States to Lübeck, Bavaria, and Hamburg
                    during the first half of the year 1897.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">And. D. White.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d178-a1.xml" xpointer="d178-a1"/>
